From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libc: __ctype_b from the native ctype table

__ctype_b, the old glibc's ctype table (before __ctype_b_loc), was looked
up in the native libc as data (DATA). An aarch64 glibc has never had it,
not even as a compat symbol, so a program linked against it got nothing:
"Global Symbol __ctype_b not found, cannot apply R_X86_64_GLOB_DAT" and a
SIGSEGV at its first isspace() (Unreal Tournament 2004's Linux build
3186: KCreateAssetDB). ctSetup() already sets my___ctype_b to
*__ctype_b_loc(), like my___ctype_tolower/toupper: DATAM gives it.

--- a/src/wrapped/wrappedlibc_private.h	2026-11-18 02:51:52.463289019 +0100
+++ b/src/wrapped/wrappedlibc_private.h	2026-11-18 02:51:52.484005126 +0100
@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@
 #ifdef STATICBUILD
 //DATA(__ctype_b, 8)
 #else
-DATA(__ctype_b, 8)
+DATAM(__ctype_b, 8)
 #endif
 GO(__ctype_b_loc, pFv)
 GO(__ctype_get_mb_cur_max, LFv)
